<?xml version='1.0' standalone='yes'?>
<!DOCTYPE PLUGIN>

<PLUGIN 
  name="motd"
  author="Sebastian Oehm"
  version="2026.10.23"
  pluginURL="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/SebastianOehm/unraid-motd/main/plugin/motd.plg"
  support="https://github.com/SebastianOehm/unraid-motd/issues"
  min="6.11.5"
  icon="fa-desktop"
>

<CHANGES>
<![CDATA[
###2026.10.23###
## New
- Docker and Compose modules: running containers whose Docker healthcheck fails are shown as `unhealthy`, and crash-looping containers as `restart loop (N)`. Compose stacks name the affected services instead, for example `unhealthy: db` or `restart loop: worker`. `check_health` (default on), `restart_warn` (default 3 restarts, `0` turns it off) and `restart_window` (default 10 minutes) control the checks, in both the `docker` and `compose` sections
- Per-module timeout: a module that takes longer than `global.timeout` seconds (default 10) is shown as "Timed out" instead of holding up the login. Set `timeout` in a module section to override it for that module, `0` turns the limit off
- Configuration reference: [CONFIGURATION.md](https://github.com/SebastianOehm/unraid-motd/blob/main/CONFIGURATION.md) describes every option with its default

## Changed
- Both new checks are on by default, so containers that run but fail their healthcheck, or that keep restarting and have only just come back up, now cause a warning where they used to show as OK. Set `check_health: false` and `restart_warn: 0` to get the old behavior
- A module that used to take longer than 10 seconds and then show up is now cut off as "Timed out". Raise its `timeout`, or set it to `0`, if it is slow but working


For older releases, see https://github.com/SebastianOehm/unraid-motd/releases
]]>
</CHANGES>

<FILE Name="/boot/config/plugins/motd/unraid-motd-2026.10.23-amd64-1.txz" Run="upgradepkg --install-new">
<URL>https://github.com/SebastianOehm/unraid-motd/releases/download/2026.10.23/unraid-motd-2026.10.23-amd64-1.txz</URL>
<SHA256>9c8811f7b835e49f80faa037c475234c26e3b9600a65e3f43418f9ce8c6e86fd</SHA256>
</FILE>

<FILE Name="/boot/config/plugins/motd/figurine_linux_amd64_v1.3.0.tar.gz">
<URL>https://github.com/arsham/figurine/releases/download/v1.3.0/figurine_linux_amd64_v1.3.0.tar.gz</URL>
<SHA256>e72430de0ca4b4b4548495d803856f5fec223f43c59a97a0bfcc714710d5032a</SHA256>
</FILE>

<!--
The 'install' script.
-->
<FILE Run="/bin/bash">
<INLINE>
<![CDATA[

tar xf /boot/config/plugins/motd/figurine_linux_amd64_v1.3.0.tar.gz -C /usr/local/bin/ --strip-components=1 deploy/figurine

# cleanup old versions
rm -f $(ls /boot/config/plugins/motd/unraid-motd-*.txz 2>/dev/null | grep -v '2026.10.23')
rm -f $(ls /boot/config/plugins/motd/figurine_linux_amd64_*.tar.gz 2>/dev/null | grep -v 'v1.3.0')

echo ""
echo "----------------------------------------------------"
echo " motd has been installed."
echo " Version: 2026.10.23"
echo "----------------------------------------------------"
echo ""
]]>
</INLINE>
</FILE>

<!--
The 'remove' script.
-->
<FILE Run="/bin/bash" Method="remove">
<INLINE>
<![CDATA[
removepkg unraid-motd

rm -f /usr/local/bin/figurine
rm -f /usr/local/bin/motd

rm -rf /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/motd
rm -rf /boot/config/plugins/motd
]]>
</INLINE>
</FILE>

</PLUGIN>
